% ============================================================================
% em-spectrum.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics em-spectrum library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what everyday thing uses
% microwaves?": it states no physics fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `band_use` rows and returns the application + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the use
% `night_vision`, recall its band — infrared). A word that is not one of the
% seven EM bands abstains honestly — the engine never invents a use.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli em-spectrum.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "em-spectrum.adj"

? band_use(radio, $Application)        % expect radio_stations
? band_use(microwave, $Application)    % expect cooking
? band_use(x_ray, $Application)        % expect teeth
? band_use($Band, night_vision)        % reverse bind — expect infrared
? band_use(sound, $Application)        % expect abstain — sound is a mechanical wave, not one of the seven EM bands
